%F A400812 Conjecture: a(n) = 13*a(n-1) - 44*a(n-2) + 28*a(n-3) + 5*a(n-4) - a(n-5) for n >= 5.
%F A400812 Conjecture: G.f.: 4*x^3*(7 + 2*x)/((1 - x)*(1 - 8*x + x^2)*(1 - 4*x - x^2)).
%F A400812 Conjecture: a(n) = A057080(n-1) - (A000045(3*n+2) - 3)/2 = A057080(n-1) - A099919(n) + 1 for n >= 1.
%F A400812 Conjecture: Limit_{n->oo} a(n)/A057080(n) = 4 - sqrt(15) = 0.1270166537... (one star triple for every 4 + sqrt(15) = 7.8729833462... tiles).
%F A400812 a(n) = A400813(n) + A400814(n) for n >= 0.
%e A400812 For a(3) = 28: the level-3 supertile (559 tiles) contains 18 major and 10 minor star triples, lying on the 14 seams of the last inflation step and forming 14 clusters: 5 of family A (1 star triple each), 1 of family B (1), 3 of family C (2 each), 2 of family D (2 each) and 3 of family E (4 each): 5*1 + 1*1 + 3*2 + 2*2 + 3*4 = 28.
%e A400812 For a(4) = 372: the level-4 supertile contains the 14 clusters created at level 4, with sizes 8, 8, 12, 15, 25, and 82 clusters created at level 3, namely 21, 8, 13, 16, 24 of families A-E: (5*8 + 1*8 + 3*12 + 2*15 + 3*25) + (21*1 + 8*1 + 13*2 + 16*2 + 24*4) = 189 + 183 = 372.
%e A400812 For a(5) = 3604: clusters created at level 5 (sizes 45, 50, 72, 87, 147), at level 4 and at level 3 give (5*45 + 1*50 + 3*72 + 2*87 + 3*147) + (21*8 + 8*8 + 13*12 + 16*15 + 24*25) + (89*1 + 63*1 + 55*2 + 126*2 + 189*4) = 1106 + 1228 + 1270 = 3604.
%Y A400812 Cf. A057080 (all tiles), A099919, A400813 (major star triples), A400814 (minor star triples).
%Y A400812 Sizes of star clusters: A397115-A397119; sizes of megaobjects: A397120, A400810, A400811.
%Y A400812 Star triples in clusters and megaobjects: A400815-A400822; numbers of megaobjects: 6*A076765, A400823, A400824.
